 }
 function render(){if(!dataset)return;const c=dataset.cohorts[cohort.value],p12=c.points.find(p=>p.month===12),check=[6,12,24].map(m=>c.points.find(p=>p.month===m));
  results.innerHTML=`<p><b>${c.n.toLocaleString()} people · ${e(c.label)}.</b> Time starts at ${e(c.origin.charAt(0).toLowerCase()+c.origin.slice(1))}.</p>${c.key==='hcc'?'<p class="allocation-small">Includes standard and nonstandard HCC applications, regardless of approval.</p>':''}${disease.value!=='hcc'?'<p class="waiting-scope">This is context for Houston access, not a waiting estimate for '+e(window.AllocationReference.diseases[disease.value].name)+'. No disease-specific estimate is available in this analysis.</p>':''}<p class="allocation-small"><b>2025 entrants have shorter follow-up.</b> Estimates account for censoring; 12–24-month results rely more on earlier entrants.</p><div class="waiting-stats"><div class="waiting-stat"><span>DDLT by 12 months</span><strong>${pct(p12.ddlt)}</strong><small>95% CI ${ci(p12,'ddlt')}</small></div><div class="waiting-stat"><span>Death / too sick by 12 months</span><strong>${pct(p12.death_or_too_sick)}</strong><small>95% CI ${ci(p12,'dropout')}</small></div><div class="waiting-stat"><span>DDLT by 24 months</span><strong>${pct(check[2].ddlt)}</strong><small>95% CI ${ci(check[2],'ddlt')}</small></div></div><div class="waiting-legend"><span>Deceased-donor transplant (DDLT)</span><span>Death / removal as too sick</span></div>${chart(c)}<p class="waiting-chart-note">Monthly cumulative-incidence estimates; shading = pointwise 95% confidence intervals. Other terminal outcomes compete with both curves.</p><div class="waiting-table-wrap"><table class="waiting-table"><caption>Outcomes from the same starting cohort</caption><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>DDLT (95% CI)</th><th>Death / too sick (95% CI)</th><th>At risk</th></tr></thead><tbody>${check.map(p=>`<tr><th>${p.month} months</th><td>${pct(p.ddlt)} (${ci(p,'ddlt')})</td><td>${pct(p.death_or_too_sick)} (${ci(p,'dropout')})</td><td>${p.at_risk}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="allocation-small">At risk = still followed on the index registration without a terminal outcome just before that time. Death/too-sick removal is not necessarily cancer progression.</p><details class="waiting-methods"><summary>How to interpret the wait time</summary><p>${c.ddlt_50pct_months===null?'Cumulative DDLT did not reach 50% during observed follow-up.':'Cumulative DDLT first reached 50% at about <b>'+c.ddlt_50pct_months+' months</b> from '+e(c.origin.charAt(0).toLowerCase()+c.origin.slice(1))+'.'} This population milestone is not a promised waiting time for an individual.</p><p>Among the ${c.recipient_only_wait.n} people who actually received DDLT before their index registration ended, median time from ${e(c.origin.charAt(0).toLowerCase()+c.origin.slice(1))} to DDLT was ${c.recipient_only_wait.median_months} months (interquartile range ${c.recipient_only_wait.q1_months}–${c.recipient_only_wait.q3_months}). <b>This recipient-only number omits people who died, were removed, or remained waiting.</b> It also favors shorter observed waits among recent entrants.</p><p>At 12 months, the estimated probability of another terminal outcome (living-donor or other/unknown-source transplant, or other removal) was ${pct(c.other_12m)}; the estimated probability of remaining without a terminal event on the index registration was ${pct(c.still_listed_12m)}. These categories explain the remaining probability.</p>${c.key==='hcc'?`<p>The median interval from index listing to the first HCC request was ${c.listing_to_request_median_months} months. Do not add group medians to estimate an individual’s total wait. Application date is not proof of exception approval or six-month clock completion.</p>`:''}<p>${c.entered_2025.toLocaleString()} people entered in 2025. Administrative censoring occurred before 12 months for ${c.censored_before_12m.toLocaleString()} people in this cohort; their observed follow-up contributes to the estimates. Follow-up ends on 31 December 2025.</p><p>Blood group, laboratory MELD, tumor course, donor acceptance and readiness can materially change an individual’s access. These pooled estimates are unadjusted.</p></details>`;
