     "divergence": "The protocol and the molecular data agree that exon 7/8 carries no added malignant risk but part company on S45, which the genotype-phenotype series treats as a special case rather than a low-risk one.",
     "proposal": "The roadmap judges the restriction defensible as organ stewardship but not as a claim about S45 biology, proposes treating S45 exon 3 as uncertain rather than low risk, and asks any NLRB narrative to say which basis applies; exon and codon must be recorded, and an immunohistochemical surrogate named as such.",
     "proposal_locator": "What we are not sure about #15; Gate 10 · Standard 'Name the qualifying route in the narrative…' (and note)",
     "rationale": "The protocol places S45 exon 3 with the exon 7/8 alterations as not qualifying the molecular route alone. The genotype-phenotype data make S45 a special case rather than a low-risk one — a weak activator in benign tumours, found at similar frequency in mutated adenomas and carcinomas, and duplicated to high activity in most carcinomas. The restriction is defensible as organ stewardship but not as a statement about risk, and the NLRB narrative should say which of the two it is.",
