     "proposal_locator": "Gate 3 · Reasonable options 'Through-the-needle microforceps biopsy' (EXPERTISE, REGISTRY) and 'Needle-based confocal laser endomicroscopy' (EXPERTISE, PROTOCOL), with local approval note; Decisions table · item 19 · why",
     "rationale": "Through-the-needle microforceps biopsy is in none of the four guidelines, its superiority claim over aspiration rests on two retrospective within-patient comparisons with an odds ratio spanning 1.12 to 67.12, and the meta-analysis's own results text states there was no significant difference in accuracy — contradicting its abstract. Needle-based confocal laser endomicroscopy is recommended against by the European guideline at GRADE 1C, and in the best training study trained readers reached only 57% sensitivity for mucinous cystic neoplasm and 65% for serous cystadenoma with interobserver agreement of kappa 0.32 and 0.44, which undercuts the economic case for it. Endoscopic ablation resolves cysts in 33 to 79% with adverse events in about 12%, has produced an adenocarcinoma after treatment, does not remove the need for surveillance, and Kyoto 2024 says it should only be performed in a clinical trial. If any of these is offered here it needs an indication, a consent form and a registry.",
     "audit": "Use of each adjunct by indication, adverse events, whether the result changed the plan, and final histology where an operation followed.",
     "web": "pcyst/#question-PCYST-D19"
    }
