   "short": "NCCN Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma v1.2026",
   "title": "National Comprehensive Cancer Network. Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma. NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology. Version 1.2026; Discussion text last updated 6 August 2026, from the extracted guideline text supplied to the programme. Premalignant Tumors of the Pancreas section. NCCN has no pancreatic cyst algorithm of its own: it summarises the international group (citing the Kyoto 2024 guidelines, PMID 38182527) and a European group (citing the superseded 2013 consensus statement, PMID 23415799, rather than the 2018 evidence-based guideline), and directs the reader to the most recent available guideline recommendations. It quotes a main-duct IPMN malignancy risk of about 62% and an MCN risk below 15%, recommends resection for main-duct IPMN of 10 mm or more and for all MCNs in operable patients, and includes IPMN and MCN with high-grade dysplasia as Tis in the AJCC 8th edition staging table.",
