     "t": "After successful downstaging no institutional stability period is added; timing follows the allocation rules (imaging ≥4 weeks after the last treatment and the 6-month wait from the first exception request).",
     "why": "Local choice resting on allocation rules, not outcome data. The 2012 international consensus noted that at least 3 months of observation after downstaging was often recommended, but that was never a randomized optimization of observation time; waiting longer may expose aggressive biology but also adds dropout and decompensation risk. Track recurrence and dropout by time from successful downstaging to transplant.",
     "setting": "standard",
     "locator": "Standard pathway document §7.4 Observation Period",
