    {
     "t": "After transplant: contrast abdominal CT/MRI and chest CT every 3–6 months for 2 years, then 6-monthly to year 5, with AFP; the explant RETREAT score guides surveillance intensity.",
     "why": "Extrapolated from a general HCC schedule and a prognostic score. The schedule follows NCCN post-treatment follow-up, which the protocol notes is not proof of an optimal transplant-specific or RETREAT-specific schedule; its review sources call risk-adapted surveillance promising but without prospective proof of the best frequency or duration. Track stage at detection of recurrence, salvage treatment and survival by RETREAT stratum.",
