    {
     "t": "Candidates need ECOG 0–1; there is no upper age limit, but those over 70 need enhanced physiologic assessment and explicit selection-committee sign-off.",
     "why": "Local rules. The protocol cites no source for ECOG 0–1. OPTN sets no age limit; the 70-year trigger and the assessment bundle (frailty, sarcopenia, cardiopulmonary, geriatric or anesthesia review) are institutional, and age alone may not be grounds to decline. The age rule cites a non-transplant eligibility cohort (Schleimer 2026); no transplant outcomes by age or performance status are cited. Track committee decisions and outcomes for these candidates.",
     "setting": "standard",
     "locator": "Standard pathway document §2.1 Inclusion Criteria",
     "refs": [
      {
       "key": "icca_comparator",
       "label": "Schleimer 2026 · non-LT comparator",
       "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41991890/"
      }
     ],
     "related": null
    },
    {
     "t": "Poorly differentiated histology is a relative contraindication.",
     "why": "Guideline-based (AASLD PSC/CCA guidance). The supporting cohort data are small and retrospective: in De Martin 2020, incidental tumors in cirrhosis, tumor grade carried a hazard ratio of 3.74. A core biopsy cannot guarantee the grade of the whole tumor, and the protocol does not define how the relative contraindication is weighed. Track biopsy versus explant grade and recurrence by grade.",
     "setting": "standard",
     "locator": "Standard pathway document §2.2 Exclusion Criteria",
