    },
    {
     "t": "For living donation, recipient staging and technical clearance are completed before irreversible donor surgery, with an explicit abort plan for occult nodes, peritoneal disease or unresectability.",
     "why": "Operational safety proposal. The protocol labels this a safety workflow, not proof that negative staging prevents recurrence. The cited UPMC series (Sethi 2026) staged recipients before donor surgery and aborted 7 of 31 explorations, but it included only seven iCCA recipients. Track aborted donor and recipient operations and occult disease found at staging.",
     "setting": "standard",
     "locator": "Standard pathway document §6.1 Staging Laparotomy",
     "refs": [
