     "related": {
      "label": "iCCA-B3 · Living-donor transplantation: study readiness",
      "href": "#high-risk-icca-b3"
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "At transplant, perihepatic lymph nodes are sampled for frozen section; extrahepatic or extrabiliary spread on frozen section aborts the transplant and the organ is reallocated.",
     "why": "Single-center protocol. The rule follows the Houston prospective case series (Lunsford 2018), in which six patients were transplanted. The protocol gives no data on frozen-section accuracy, and it notes that negative EUS sampling does not exclude all nodal disease. Track agreement between frozen-section and final pathology, and aborted transplants.",
     "setting": "standard",
     "locator": "Standard pathway document §6.1 Staging Laparotomy",
     "refs": [
      {
       "key": "lunsford",
       "label": "Lunsford 2018 · Houston",
       "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29548617/"
      }
     ],
     "related": null
    },
    {
     "t": "No routine adjuvant therapy after a complete pathologic response; with residual viable tumor, chemotherapy is considered only case by case or within a prospective protocol.",
     "why": "Extrapolated. The protocol states that no post-transplant adjuvant standard exists and that benefit and tolerability in immunosuppressed recipients are unproven; the cited source is a single-center case series (Lunsford 2018). Track adjuvant use, tolerance and recurrence by explant response.",
     "setting": "standard",
     "locator": "Standard pathway document §8 Adjuvant Therapy Post-Transplant; decision 'Transplant and follow-up'",
     "refs": [
