    {
     "t": "After confirmed recurrence, transplant hepatology, surgery and oncology discuss individualized immunosuppression minimization.",
     "why": "Single-center retrospective association. In the cited cohort (Gül-Klein 2022: 67 recipients with mixed CCA subtypes, 1988–2022), restrictive immunosuppression was associated with longer survival after recurrence, but selection and confounding limit causal inference, and mTOR use showed no independent association. The protocol supports consideration, not automatic withdrawal or routine mTOR substitution. Track rejection and survival after minimization.",
