     "related": {
      "label": "HEHE-B2 · Extrahepatic disease and vascular invasion",
      "href": "#high-risk-hehe-b2"
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "No neoadjuvant or bridging regimen is required; the sarcoma–transplant MDT chooses observation, ablation, embolization, radiation or systemic therapy case by case.",
     "why": "Expert consensus. The international EHE consensus supports active surveillance for stable disease and individual treatment choice. The only comparison cited is a 50-patient single-center series in which five-year survival from diagnosis did not differ by initial strategy; the groups were small and clinically selected, so this is not equivalence, and 14 of 25 patients first observed progressed. Track progression and dropout by pre-transplant strategy.",
     "setting": "standard",
     "locator": "Standard pathway document §7 Pretransplant treatment and stability",
     "refs": [
